  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn ichidan ({一段|いちだん}) transitive verb. Takes を to mark the body part or abstract thing being hurt.\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {痛|いた}める: to hurt, to injure (physical pain or emotional distress)\n- {傷|いた}める: to damage, to wound, to spoil (physical damage to objects or food)\n- {炒|いた}める: to stir-fry (cooking)\nAll three are pronounced いためる but have different meanings and kanji.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {腰|こし}を{痛|いた}める: to hurt one's back\n- {膝|ひざ}を{痛|いた}める: to injure one's knee\n- {頭|あたま}を{痛|いた}める: to worry, to agonize\n- {心|こころ}を{痛|いた}める: to be pained, to feel sorrow\n- {胃|い}を{痛|いた}める: to upset one's stomach (from stress)",
